---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Accurate Drawing Skills — Supply List">
  <div class="home">
    <h3 class="page-category">Online workshop</h3>
    <h1>Accurate Drawing Skills</h1>
    <h2>Supply list</h2>

    <h4>Paper</h4>
    <p>Really any paper around A4 or 8.5×11″ will work for this workshop! I'd recommend any cheap paper you don't mind drawing on. I actually just use regular printer paper!</p>

    <h4>Pencils</h4>
    <p>Any HB, F, or H pencil you like drawing with. Even a #2 pencil works!</p>

    <h4>Eraser</h4>
    <p>A kneaded eraser</p>
    <p>Optional: A pen-style eraser like the <a href="https://www.dickblick.com/items/tombow-mono-zero-refillable-eraser-round-single/">Tombow Mono Zero Round</a>.</p>

    <h4>Measuring tool</h4>
    <p>Anything long and straight will do. Try a few different things and see what you like. Some ideas:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Knitting needle</li>
      <li>Skewer</li>
      <li>The pencil you're drawing with</li>
      <li>Ruler</li>
      <li>String</li>
      <li>Straightedge</li>
    </ul>

    <h4>Board</h4>
    <p>Any drawing board will do—or even a clipboard!</p>

    <h4>Printer (optional)</h4>
    <p>A printer isn't necessary, but will be helpful for printing out worksheets.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
